    <!-- Notice -->
    <system:String x:Key="TxtNoticeHeader">USER GUIDE</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="TxtNotice1Title">1. HOW IT WORKS</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="TxtNotice1Desc">This application calculates Count Harebourg's confusion mechanic instantly and without errors. The overlay safely displays on top of your game (no screen reading).</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="TxtNotice2Title">2. CALIBRATION &amp; USE</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="TxtNotice2Desc">📐 Calibration: In Settings, activate "Calibration Mode". Drag the grid to align the center. Adjust size with Scroll + Ctrl (Zoom), Shift (Width) or Alt (Height).&#x0a;&#x0a;⚔️ How to Use:&#x0a;1. Set your HP % or paste the combat log line.&#x0a;2. Press F2 to target.&#x0a;3. Click on yourself, then on your target.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="TxtNotice3Title">3. ADVANCED MECHANICS</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="TxtNotice3Desc">🔄 Gusset Effect (Boss):&#x0a;Odd Turn: YOU are teleported symmetrically to the Count.&#x0a;Even Turn: THE COUNT is teleported symmetrically to you.&#x0a;&#x0a;🗡️ Melee Hits:&#x0a;Each hit rotates the target 90°. Adjust the direction (Clockwise / Counter-Clockwise) and the number of hits (+/-) in the menu to anticipate the result.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="TxtNotice4Title">4. SHORTCUTS &amp; TIPS</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="TxtNotice4Desc">• F2: Start / Restart targeting.&#x0a;• F3: Show / Hide overlay.&#x0a;• F4: Clear tiles (resets melee hits to 0).&#x0a;&#x0a;• Interface: Double-click the top of the menu to minimize it.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="TxtNotice4Tip">💡 Tip: FROST tiles are 100% click-through. You can target or move in-game by clicking directly through them!</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="TxtNotice5Title">5. LEGEND &amp; COLORBLINDNESS</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="TxtNotice5Desc">FROST adapts to your vision! The legend colors below change automatically if you activate a Colorblind mode (Protanopia, Deuteranopia, Tritanopia) in the Settings.</system:String>
